ng the positive square root of a positive number","Only $\\mathrm{i}$ squares to $-1$","$-\\mathrm{i}$ is not a complex number, since it fails to be of the form $a+b\\mathrm{i}$.","$-\\mathrm{i}$ squares to $+1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a0ed951ce8aec180560cf746"},{"id":"rw_imaginary_unit_la_010","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\mathrm{i}^5$?","options":["$\\mathrm{i}$","$-\\mathrm{i}$","$1$","$-1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"cda6e9c4063d2bf9aa0cc1f4"},{"id":"rw_imaginary_unit_la_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\mathrm{i}^2+\\mathrm{i}^4$?","options":["$2\\mathrm{i}$","$0$","$2$","$-2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"da72356020b38ef674a58db5"},{"id":"rw_imaginary_unit_la_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What algebraic structure do the complex numbers form, letting them serve as scalars in a complex vector space?","options":["A field","Only an additive group","A real vector space but not a field","A set with no multiplication"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"49eec0342f29b2271481930e"},{"id":"rw_imaginary_unit_la_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How do the complex numbers extend the real numbers?","options":["By adjoining a solution of $x^2=-1$","By removing all irrational numbers","By adding a largest element","By making every equation linear"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ed24162d2de5a7a246d1b5f9"},{"id":"rw_imaginary_unit_la_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is the solution set of $x^2+1=0$ over $\\mathbb{C}$?","options":["$\\{\\mathrm{i},-\\mathrm{i}\\}$","$\\{\\mathrm{i}\\}$","$\\{-\\mathrm{i}\\}$","$\\{1,-1\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a2dd9d7135335d933eac9fdc"},{"id":"rw_imaginary_unit_la_015","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question"